## Scope

Documentation-only follow-up after PR #42 merged the executable next-generation transition-pair core and experimental angular calibration.

`docs/NEXT_GENERATION_RESEARCH_STATUS.md` was still describing the superseded prospective-thought architecture and unresolved SD semantics. This PR updates that status note to match the current authoritative private design and the code already present on public `main`.

### Updated status

- microscopic nextgen search coordinate is retrospective `(m, ΔU)`; `Q` is context only;
- prospective thought is intervention proposal only;
- active frontier uses unused completed transitions with parent→child replacement;
- `U = V + SD`, with `SD = 1/sqrt(N rho)` from current live frontier geometry;
- `V` means expected whole-frontier displacement and realized return is direct `MMD²/2` with no null subtraction;
- current RBF median-bandwidth realization remains runnable but is explicitly under theoretical calibration audit;
- frozen empirical angular calibration `C_0(c)=2F_0(c)-1` exists as an experimental geometry layer and is not wired into controller occupancy yet;
- old prospective-thought + null-adjusted 12-pair assumptions are marked superseded;
- open/nonblocking and experiment-gated items are updated accordingly.

### Boundary

No production code changes. `src/dte_backend/**` is untouched. The already-merged `src/dte_nextgen/**` implementation remains unchanged.

Keep this PR draft until CI confirms the repository/bundle boundary remains green.

