## Summary

Keeps the Firecrawl bearer token inside its exact HTTPS trust boundary and bounds crawl/pagination work.

- allow the token only to `https://api.firecrawl.dev` on the standard HTTPS port, rejecting userinfo, explicit ports and every other origin;
- validate the initial URL and each service-provided `next` URL before a request;
- disable Requests redirects and fail on every 3xx without contacting its target;
- add a per-request timeout, whole-crawl polling deadline and pagination page cap;
- stop on terminal failed/cancelled crawl states;
- validate response shape (`dict` page and list `data`);
- translate timeout, transport, HTTP and invalid-JSON failures into bounded non-reflective errors that contain no URL, headers, response body or signed cursor;
- keep response bodies out of logs.

## User impact

Normal Firecrawl pagination is unchanged. Untrusted destinations, redirects, malformed pagination links, terminal failures and unbounded waits now stop safely.

## Verification at `9d94c5ca0ac3b7a7874f35eedbd608259b1fb768`

- `uv run --with pytest python -m pytest tests/test_firecrawl_pagination.py tests/test_firecrawl_safety.py -q` — 10 tests and 8 subtests passed;
- mocked coverage includes malicious initial/subsequent links, cross-origin redirect no-follow/no-token-forwarding, non-reflective timeout/connection/HTTP failures, invalid data and page cap;
- Black and isort (Black profile) checks passed;
- `git diff --check` passed.

No external API or production service was contacted.

## Summary
Implements the runtime foundation of accepted ADR-042.

## Behavior
- derives a canonical control regime from Zendure requested/actual mode;
- NOM (`delegated_bidirectional`) tolerates transient flow oscillations and only raises a contradiction after 120 s of sustained PV + battery discharge + export;
- Slim ontladen (`delegated_discharge_only`) validates P1 baseline tracking using <50 W green, 50–150 W grey, >150 W red;
- red becomes actionable after 120 s, grey after 300 s;
- regime changes reset timers;
- standby validates battery power around zero rather than grid baseline;
- elapsed time replaces sample-count semantics;
- current flow observation now carries regime/band/timer evidence into the Planning Input Snapshot;
- observer remains evidence-only and cannot switch control directly.

## Tests
Updates live flow observer regression tests for NOM transient behavior, 120 s NOM contradiction, Slim ontladen hysteresis/timers, regime reset and standby semantics.

## Runtime
