Aligns the G18 sovereign-runtime worker with the canonical engine-v11 fail-closed/active-worker invariant.

Changes:
- removes legacy `may_remain_blocked` semantics from the missing-sovereign-node path;
- emits a machine-readable `CONDITIONAL_CONSTRAINT` resolution contract when the current worker cannot create/identify an eligible node within its authority ceiling;
- names `REPOSITORY_OWNER` as the next resolution level with explicit capabilities, workaround candidates, completion evidence, and next action;
- changes the expected transition to `DERIVE_AND_REGISTER_RESOLUTION_TASK` so engine v11 creates active successor work instead of passively rechecking the same physical-resource condition;
- preserves hosted-environment rejection and zero GitHub-token production/runtime authority;
- adds deterministic worker tests for both missing-node and hosted-environment collision behavior.

Canonical owners: #59 / #65. Live activation still requires a declared StegVerse-owned/federated node and nine-predicate activation proof; this PR does not claim product activation.

Tanpa URL / Auto Source only.

Root cause from runtime screenshots: the shared renderer rejects any structured body that cannot fit its existing max-4-line body box. The simple Auto Source writer allowed denser 10-24 word bodies, so valid factual content could reach rendering and fail with `Body tidak muat dalam maksimal empat baris.` across unrelated topics.

This PR does not modify images.js or shared renderer behavior. Instead it adds an Auto Source-only visual-fit guard after factual composition/fact-check and before rendering:
- compact body conservatively to <=16 words / ~140 chars;
- compact optional bullets to <=7 words;
- keep titles within the existing structured layout range;
- synchronize claim.text after compaction while retaining the same sourceId/evidence;
- preserve 0-3 bullet flexibility;
- run only when sourceMode === auto.

Pakai URL remains exact pass-through and does not load the guard. No UI, renderer, template, CSS, sourceUrlFinalizer, or generation.js changes.

